VERDICT: one NIRSpec IFU velocity field per target delivers the velocity half (rotation gate, inclination, V_c).
The gas mass decides the test. With the full-kernel amplification at the gate, JWST alone gives ~2 sigma on CONST vs HUBBLE
(three objects) and no decision on CONST vs LCDM; a 0.12-dex gas mass lifts CONST vs HUBBLE past 3 sigma. The decisive
CONST-vs-LCDM measurement needs gas masses AND more objects. The framework's own z~2 zero point still carries the open
L189 retained-halo correction (not computed here).

